      "id": 1,
      "text": "Latah takes its name from the nearby creek, a native word meaning “stream where little fish are caught.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latah%2C_Washington"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first wave of settlers arrived in 1872, including the Wimpy and Coplan families who helped establish the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latah%2C_Washington"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1880, a prehistoric mammoth bone was unearthed just west of Latah, sparking early paleontological interest.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.palousescenicbyway.org/latah"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Coplan brothers uncovered mammoth fossils in 1876 near the creek, bringing scientific attention to the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latah%2C_Washington"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "After finding fossils, the Coplan brothers toured their discoveries through Washington, Idaho, and Oregon, sharing the region’s ancient history.",
